  body: "# Severe Disablement Allowance continuation after closure\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe SDA introduction
    says the non-contributory benefit ceased to be available to new claimants from 6 April 2001 while specified
    previous or existing entitlement could continue.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nThe continuation conditions differ
    according to age at the transition and the period of incapacity. This does not open a present SDA claim route,
    transfer criteria to ESA or infer that every historical award still continues.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n\
    - [DMG 57001, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a818c4440f0b62302697e6e/dmgch57.pdf#page=5).\n\
    - [DMG 57002, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a818c4440f0b62302697e6e/dmgch57.pdf#page=5).\n\
    - [DMG 57003, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a818c4440f0b62302697e6e/dmgch57.pdf#page=5).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch57`:
    PDF `e5308157f4aed131c245dfd1554a126ad2800f670127de7995f6c643db8ce63b`; extracted pages `5b68aac36596be58528e0c3561d5ef604ec3cf774a61eb2ab93d8639dca9531c`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.506330Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a818c4440f0b62302697e6e/dmgch57.pdf#page=5
